Title: fullcite
Bibliography: refs.bib
Bibliography style: chicago
Resolve citations: true
------------------------------------

An inline \fullcite{Quine:1948} sits inside its paragraph, with prose
following it — so the outer element must be a `span.fullcite`, not a div
(a div would close the `<p>` in the browser and orphan this text).

Two keys at once: \fullcite{Quine:1948,Skyrms:1996}, one `.csl-entry` each.

\fullcite{NoSuchKey} emits nothing at all.

@bibliography{title="References"}
